A||||12||Mach10||Ready to start N-dropping my car to DEATH.||||8||
Z||000000||Mach10||05-26-2001||05:29 PM||||I am very frustrated at the total lack of options for my 3-speed slushbox   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> :|<P>I'm happy with what the 2.8 puts out at the moment, but it makes me want to cry whenever I hit 2nd, and I drop below the powerband.. I need to do something about this, and soon.<P>First of all, I probably need a better unit than the TH125 3-speed. Anyone have any suggestions? I don't care about number of gears, nor top-speed, but I need a better launch, and a little more go. If the tires can slip, fine, I can adjust driving style.<P>If I can't get a better transmission, and NO, I'm not at this point willing to do a manual-swap, then I need some suggestions as to what I can do with my current (or a spare TH125   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) transmission? I <B>REALLY</B> want a better final drive. Something like 3.33 or 3.6X would be nice. 4.10 is a little much. Where can I get these DAMN gears?!?! I cannot find them ANYWHERE! I have no problem tearing down a transmission, but the number(lack therein) of options with this transmission is absurd.<P>**<B>MACH10 IS FRUSTRATED</B>**<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 05-26-2001).]||206.126.176.10||reg||8
Z||000001||Mach10||05-26-2001||07:35 PM||||<B><I>BuMp</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Songman||05-26-2001||07:41 PM||||You can put in one of the later model 4-speed automatics. It is not a direct fit and requires quite a bit of change. And it will probably be just as 'slushy' or maybe even more than what you already have..<P>There are a few here that have it and it has been discussed on the forum. Do a search on 4T60E and it should bring up some things for you to read until someone that has one of these responds.<P>I plan to put one of these in one of my cars as well..<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||PBJ||05-26-2001||07:42 PM||||Have you tried to adjust the T.V. cable from throttle to trans.  I know you can have a shift kit put into the 125.  I don't know about a higher stall torque converter but that sounds like what you are looking for.  There is also the newer 4sp auto in the 97 and up sunfire, cav's, and g/am, carlines||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mach10||05-26-2001||08:20 PM||||Actually, the shifting itself isn't too bad. Fairly clean and quick. My problem is with the gearing, or at least the final drive. The different torque converter idea has some merit, however.<P>I really don't care how many gears I end up with. The 4spds are not much better geared than our beloved (&gt;:|)th-125. I've done some searching on the matter, but haven't found anything really relevant. I guess what I want is a different final drive. The shifting characteristics of the th-125 aren't too bad. It's the gearing that's killer.<P>Does anyone know what I could do with the kickdown cable to increas line pressure a little? I'd like shifts to be at a higher rpm.<p>[This message has been edited by Mach10 (edited 05-26-2001).]||206.126.176.10||reg||6
Z||000005||fropuff||05-26-2001||08:36 PM||||If you're talking about getting better take-off when racing, you can manually shift the auto.  I just shift at 5500 to second, ~4700 to third.  Seems to help quite a bit, IMO.||||reg||10
Z||000006||Mach10||05-26-2001||08:47 PM||||I take 'er up to 5300, myself. That's not the issue. The car pulls fine when in the powerband. Problem is that the first gear is WAY too tall for this motor. I'm thinking that the higher-stall converter may be the route, if I can't find a gearset.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mach10||05-26-2001||11:52 PM||||*nudge<BR>Someone MUST know where to find final drive assemblies!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000008||KRMFiero||05-27-2001||08:19 AM||||for my 4.5 swap i am using the TH440T   4 speed auto out of a 88 Cadilliac, to mount this you only need to buy a trans mount for a  89 pontiac 6000 2.8 Auto... and it will bolt right to the original trans mount spot and use fiero axles... i'm pretty sure it will work with other engines too<P>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000009||Mathias||05-27-2001||10:32 AM||||Just get a higher stall converter. I had done this a number of years ago before I discovered the joy's of a standard tranny. What it basically does is allow the engine to rev up a bit higher on the takeoff, putting it closer to the meat of the powerband, giving you a nice bit of extra push.||||reg||1
Z||000010||theogre||05-27-2001||01:42 PM||||The only place you'll get diferant final gears is from a tranny shop or from a used tranny. Even then there aren't many choices. <P>That I know of, There are no alternates for the gearing beyond changing finals.||||reg||1
Z||000011||p4n1c||05-27-2001||02:23 PM||||My recommendation is either the TH440T4 like in the 88 w-bodies and a couple other GM cars or the 4T60(which is the renamed TH440T4).  I think it would be your best bet over the 4T60-E which is electronic, it should be easier to substitute the vacuum controlled TH440/4T60 over the 4T60-E into a Fiero(correct me if I'm wrong).<P>The TH440 is in my Cutlass and I can say that it is a very good transmission and just got rebuilt after 400,000kms(250,000 miles)(The OD gear looked like someone hacksawed through a quarter of it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket" :D||||reg||1
Z||000012||Mach10||05-28-2001||01:55 AM||||Coolness. How is the gearing on a 4T60? Besides having that nice Overdrive thing, how does it stack up?||||reg||7
